Built from, and only from:
- the `initialize` answer of `npx -y @agentclientprotocol/codex-acp@2.1.1`,
  received live on 2026-10-02 (agentInfo @agentclientprotocol/codex-acp
  2.1.1; sign-in method details dropped);
- the adapter's own scenario baseline at its v2.1.1 tag,
  src/__tests__/scenarios/data/baseline/plain/command-approval.jsonl
  (codeload.github.com/agentclientprotocol/codex-acp, tag v2.1.1, fetched
  2026-10-02): its session/new answer, its notifications, its permission
  request and its prompt answer, in its order, unchanged except
  "session-1" -> s-1 and /workspace -> /work. That baseline is what the
  adapter emits for the "plain" client profile against a scripted Codex
  app-server, not a live model.

Added by hand around it, as the JSON-RPC envelope a client sends: the
client's initialize, session/new and session/prompt requests (Devplane's
declared capabilities), the request ids, and the client's answer to the
permission (allow_once, as the scenario answered it).

The session opens in `agent` (Auto review) — the adapter's start when
nothing is configured — and its mode config option offers read-only,
workspace-write, agent and agent-full-access.

The call: a `tool_call` carrying title "npm install", kind execute and its
input, then a permission request titled "Run command" carrying the same input.
Later-input update observed: no (the scenario sends the input with the
first report).
